This code has a real bug: `log.Fatal` calls `os.Exit(1)`, so a single malformed request would kill the entire metrics-router process — that's a self-inflicted DoS from any client sending bad input.

Fix: return an HTTP error instead.

```go
func handlePolicy(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    policy, err := decodeAndValidate(r.Body)
    if err != nil {
        http.Error(w, "invalid route policy: "+err.Error(), http.StatusBadRequest)
        return
    }
    publish(policy)
}
```

Also worth flagging back to Wes: this repo's convention explicitly prohibits `log.Fatal` in handlers, so this would need to change before merge regardless of the severity argument. Want me to draft that as a PR comment?
